then work together.

00:27:16.970 --> 00:27:22.300
My team built a package
that helps us handle our internal

00:27:22.300 --> 00:27:24.760
S3 credentials

00:27:24.760 --> 00:27:28.330
so that the app has the
service account credentials.

00:27:28.330 --> 00:27:31.900
The app has access to S3
as part of setting up our

00:27:31.900 --> 00:27:35.500
environment variables. So that was
the first thing that we did.

00:27:35.500 --> 00:27:38.500
That didn't make it so that
the individual user needed to have

00:27:38.500 --> 00:27:42.130
the right S3 access
to the bucket.

00:27:42.130 --> 00:27:45.730
And then I also--
I'll say invented. Nobody invented

00:27:45.730 --> 00:27:48.100
this-- but invented
it for this app.

00:27:48.100 --> 00:27:49.750
We've got the Submit button.

00:27:49.750 --> 00:27:53.670
And we also have a Save
For Later button where,

00:27:53.670 --> 00:27:56.730
in terms of just like
naming these files, it's like, OK,

00:27:56.730 --> 00:27:58.500
