00:40:45.520 --> 00:40:49.040
your provider
arrangement looks like.

00:40:49.040 --> 00:40:52.090
So for us, on the
backend, that's part of plan design.

00:40:52.090 --> 00:40:54.910
So if we're going to say
these members can sign up for this

00:40:54.910 --> 00:40:59.130
kind of network within
this value-based care arrangement,

00:40:59.130 --> 00:41:00.450
we still--

00:41:00.450 --> 00:41:02.760
there might be different
premiums associated with that,

00:41:02.760 --> 00:41:06.360
different aspects of the plan
design that feed the risk

00:41:06.360 --> 00:41:08.880
adjustment transfers.

00:41:08.880 --> 00:41:12.030
So what that comes down to,
in terms of risk adjustment,

00:41:12.030 --> 00:41:17.680
is understanding the population that
is participating in that plan.

00:41:17.680 --> 00:41:21.270
So different people may choose
to select different plans based

00:41:21.270 --> 00:41:25.830
on their own personal needs
on the marketplace. And so

00:41:25.830 --> 00:41:29.460
understanding what is driving
whatever subset of members to

00:41:29.460 --> 00:41:32.940
enroll in these plans is really
where some of the analytics

00:41:32.940 --> 00:41:36.690
that our risk adjustment
actuarial team is doing. Because

00:41:36.690 --> 00:41:38.970
of how you price it,
how you design that,

00:41:38.970 --> 00:41:40.780
then you come back
and say, OK, well,

00:41:40.780 --> 00:41:42.780
what is the risk
of these members?

00:41:46.850 --> 00:41:47.780
- Thank you.

